    "result_text": "Done. The build is green \u2014 all tests pass (`Tests run: 3, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).\n\n## What I did\n\nIntroduced address normalization applied whenever an owner is created (`POST /api/owners`).\n\n**New \u2014 `AddressNormalizer`** (`rest/function/owner/AddressNormalizer.java`): a shared, idempotent `normalize(String)` that trims, collapses internal whitespace, upper-cases, and expands whole-word abbreviations (`ST`\u2192`STREET`, `RD`\u2192`ROAD`, `AVE`\u2192`AVENUE`). Tokenizing by space means it only touches whole words, so `STREET` isn't re-expanded and applying it to an already-normalized value is a no-op.\n\n**Store & return the normalized address** \u2014 `ValidateOwnerRequiredFields` (the single body-binding, first step) now normalizes the address in place and republishes the DTO. Because it's republished, everything downstream (`BuildOwner` \u2192 entity \u2192 `SaveOwner` \u2192 the `GET` response) sees the normalized form.\n\n**Required-field check on the normalized value** \u2014 since the address is normalized before the blank check in that same step, an address that is blank after normalization (e.g. `\"   \"`) is rejected as a missing field \u2192 400.\n\n**Every address comparison uses the normalized form** \u2014 `EnsureUniqueHousehold` (duplicate detection) and `AssignHousehold` (shared household id derivation + matching) now compare/derive the address via `AddressNormalizer.normalize`, applied to both the request and each existing owner, so seed/legacy addresses are judged in the same canonical form. Last-name comparison is unchanged.\n\nThe three acceptance tests confirm the behavior: `\"  12  main  st \"` \u2192 `\"12 MAIN STREET\"`, `\"7 elm ave\"` \u2192 `\"7 ELM AVENUE\"`, and `\"   \"` \u2192 400.",
